course: dictionary
lesson: 6501
title: Words for things we wear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A necklace is a piece of jewellery you wear around your neck. It is often a chain or a string of beads. «Take off rings, earrings and necklaces before sport, because they can catch and tear skin.» Rings and earrings are jewellery too, so a necklace is a thing you wear.
explain: Use the words around it to check your meaning. «Toadspawn comes in long strings like a necklace with a double row of eggs.» The eggs are in a line, wrapped around plants, so a necklace must be something with beads or parts strung along a string.
explain: A necklace can be made from many things: shells, pearls, flowers, beads or gold. «When Maddie gives Lily half a "best friend" necklace, Chloe's face drops.» Here the necklace is a gift, and it shows how someone feels. Necklace is a noun, and its plural is necklaces.
fact: Necklace is a noun. Its plural is necklaces.
fact: A necklace is a piece of jewellery worn around the neck, often a chain or a string of beads.
fact: A necklace can be made of shells, pearls, flowers, beads or gold.
fact: Common phrases are «wear a necklace», «a gold necklace», «a pearl necklace» and «a bead necklace».
fact: In maths, a necklace can be a set made from a number of beads, such as beads per necklace.
exercise: «Take off rings, earrings and necklaces before sport.» What is a necklace? | *A piece of jewellery worn around the neck | A kind of shoe worn for running | A type of sport played in water | A sort of bread
exercise: «Toadspawn comes in long strings like a necklace with a double row of eggs.» What does the word necklace help you picture? | A tall tree on a hill | A bag full of sand | A loud crowd cheering at a match | *Eggs in a long row, like beads on a string
exercise: Which of these can a necklace be made from? | *Pearls | Thunder | Bricks | Sand dunes
test: Which word is the plural of necklace? | necklace | *necklaces | necklacing | necklacely
test: Which phrase names a necklace made of pearls? | *a pearl necklace | a pearl hat | a pearl shoe | a pearl ring
exam: Which sentence uses necklace correctly? | The necklace ran across the football pitch. | The necklace was very loudly sad. | *She wore a gold necklace to the party. | He ate three necklaces for breakfast.
